{'symbol': 'AWK', 'date': '2022-11-29 16:48:00', 'title': 'NEW JERSEY AMERICAN WATER AND APEX SOLUTIONS GROUP HOST GRADUATION CEREMONY FOR “WATER UP!” TRAINING PROGRAM', 'text': "CAMDEN, N.J.--( BUSINESS WIRE )--TODAY, NEW JERSEY AMERICAN WATER HOSTED A GRADUATION CEREMONY FOR ITS SECOND COHORT OF WATER UTILITY PIPELINE (WATER UP!) TRAINING PROGRAM GRADUATES IN PARTNERSHIP WITH APEX SOLUTIONS GROUP. OVER 11 WEEKS OF FIELD TRAINING AND CLASSROOM-BASED CURRICULUM, 13 ADULTS, MOSTLY FROM PLAINFIELD, LEARNED ABOUT THE WATER UTILITY INDUSTRY, NEW JERSEY AMERICAN WATER'S ROLE, AND ESSENTIAL BUSINESS SKILLS NECESSARY TO SUCCESSFULLY PURSUE A CAREER IN THE INDUSTRY UPON GRADUATION."}{'symbol': 'AWK', 'date': '2022-11-29 11:30:00', 'title': 'AMERICAN WATER ANNOUNCES $1 MILLION COMMITMENT TO STUDENTS CONTINUING EDUCATION THROUGH A NEW INCLUSION AND DIVERSITY SCHOLARSHIP PROGRAM', 'text': 'CAMDEN, N.J.--( BUSINESS WIRE )--AMERICAN WATER (NYSE: AWK), THE LARGEST PUBLICLY TRADED U.S. WATER AND WASTEWATER UTILITY COMPANY, ANNOUNCED TODAY A $1 MILLION COMMITMENT OVER FOUR YEARS TO UNDERSERVED AND UNDERREPRESENTED STUDENTS CONTINUING EDUCATION THROUGH A NEW INCLUSION AND DIVERSITY (“I&D”) SCHOLARSHIP PROGRAM.'}